# SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-3.0-or-later
#
# Controller input for Killzone (SCES-52004), from power-on through the menus
# into the first level of the campaign, and three and a half minutes of play
# there: across the battlefield under fire until the player is killed, then
# Retry and a little more. A script for ps2n-host -pad
# (scripts/windows/game.ps1 -Pad). The frame numbers are those of a run with
# no memory card in either slot; run it for 17,500 frames.
#
# This file holds button presses, written for PS2Native's tests. Nothing in
# it comes from the game. What each press is for was found by looking at the
# pictures of runs under stock PCSX2 (scripts/windows/sheets.ps1).
#
# frame  input  frames held

# "No memory card (PS2) found ... Do you want to start the game?": Continue.
1900    cross     4
# The intro film: skip it. The title screen follows.
2300    cross     4
# The title screen: to the main menu (Options, Game, Extras).
2500    start     4
# Game, then Campaign. The game looks for a memory card and asks for a profile.
2900    cross     4
3300    cross     4

# "Create profile": edit the profile name. The game's keyboard takes a letter
# when a direction is held and a button pressed meanwhile: three letters.
3700    cross     4
3800    up        60
3830    cross     4
3900    l_up      60
3930    cross     4
4000    l_left    60
4030    cross     4
# With no direction held, Cross is "enter": the name is done.
4200    cross     4
# Down to "Create profile", and create it.
4300    down      30
4450    cross     4
# "Do you want to save this profile to the memory card?": No.
4700    triangle  4

# Select level (the first), difficulty (Normal), character (the first).
5000    cross     4
5300    cross     4
5600    cross     4
# The level's opening scene: skip it. The level loads until about frame 6,600.
5900    cross     4

# In the level: walk, look, fire, crouch, reload, zoom.
6700    l_up      300
6900    r1        60
7050    r_right   40
7150    l_up      250
7200    r1        30
7300    l3        60
7450    circle    4
7500    r_left    60
7600    l_up      300
7700    r1        100
7900    r3        4
8000    l_right   100
8150    r1        50
8300    l_up      400
8500    r_up      30
8600    r1        120
8800    triangle  4
8850    l_left    100
# The view level again, then out of the trench and across the battlefield.
8960    r_down    30
9000    l_up      600
9200    r_right   30
9300    r1        40
9700    l_up      500
9800    r_left    50
10000   r1        80
10300   l_up      600
10400   square    4
10600   r1        60
11000   l_left    200
11100   r_right   60
11300   l_up      700
11500   r1        100
11800   l2        4
12100   l_up      800
12300   r_right   80
12500   r1        150
13000   l_up      900
13200   r_left    80
13500   r1        100
14000   l_up      900
14300   r1        200

# The player is killed at about frame 14,000; "Failed" is up from 14,500.
# Retry, and "Save progression?": Cancel. The level starts again at once.
15200   cross     4
15500   triangle  4
16600   l_up      300
16800   r1        60
17100   r_right   60
17200   r1        60
